    "note": "e2e_ms: from this node's receipt of a pilot message (the /vla/action_4d callback's entry, time.monotonic_ns) to the publication on /shield/setpoint of the first setpoint flown from it. With --tick-trigger action the tick runs on the message's arrival, so e2e is the tick's own work up to the publication, plus a deferral only for a message that arrived within min_gap_s of the previous tick (tick_schedule). Not in it: the DDS hop from the pilot's publish to the callback (the message carries no stamp) and what follows the publication (the adapter's NED conversion, MAVROS, the autopilot)"
